# Model routing (Cursor)

Tokens are a budget. The **chat model** (coordinator) keeps understand /
design / plan / review / report. Pure implementation goes to a `Task`
subagent with a **cheap** catalog slug — not the same Anthropic (or other)
frontier model as the chat.

## Rules

1. **Only slugs from this turn’s `available_subagent_models` catalog.** Never
   invent `claude-*` / Anthropic names if they are not listed. If the catalog
   has no cheap option, use `inherit`.
2. **Do not force Anthropic (or any one vendor) for every Task.** Pick by job:

| Work | Cursor `Task` `model` |
| --- | --- |
| `camstack-implementer`, `camstack-test-fixer`, `camstack-docs-writer` | cheapest non-`inherit` (today usually `composer-2.5-fast`) |
| `camstack-ui-engineer` (build the UI) | same cheap slug |
| Look at `ui:shots` PNGs / visual sign-off | coordinator (`inherit` / chat) — Read the PNGs |
| `camstack-diagnostician`, `code-reviewer`, Bugbot, Security Review | `inherit` |
| Tiny edit cheaper than writing a brief | coordinator, no Task |

3. **Never `general-purpose`** for camstack work — use the project agents
   above (or name the skills to load). See `camstack-tdd-review.mdc`.
4. Claude Code agent frontmatter (`model: sonnet|haiku|opus`) is for that
   harness only; on Cursor map through the table, do not copy those names
   unless they appear in the catalog.

Source of truth for the table: `.claude/skills/camstack-workflow/SKILL.md`
